# fitshead (long list) of a 16-bit FITS image (img16.fits, from mkdata.py;
# fitshead only reads BITPIX=16), listed twice into the same text file: the
# first run creates it (table header and one line), the second one appends a
# line. In 5.1 both runs stopped with a gfortran runtime error (writing after
# reading the file to the end without BACKSPACE); the reference was created
# with the fixed code.
outputs = head.txt
--- run fitshead
0
img16.fits
head.txt
l
y
y
--- run fitshead
0
img16.fits
head.txt
l
y
y
